  "properties": {
    "title": "Escaping the cell grid: Terminal GIS",
    "description": "For some of us, terminal windows are ubiquitous. Whether we love them or just find them convenient, there's always one open. However, we best know them as grids of text. Can we escape this 80x25 prison and build something that resembles an interactive GIS application?\r\n\r\nDuring this talk, we'll take a look at some terminal protocol extensions and libraries in the Rust ecosystem.",
